      },
      {
        order = 43,
        marker = "*",
        depth = 1,
        instruction = "To experience the weather of one of the seven colors, you must enter the area while the weather is active, you will receive a brief cutscene confirming the weather effect.",
        action = "travel",
        entities = {  },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 44,
        marker = "**",
        depth = 2,
        instruction = "To know the weather of the area you are in, check the top left corner of where your compass (above the day/time/pos in the bottom left of your screen - assuming you have it toggled-on by using /clock )",
        action = "note",
        entities = {  },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 45,
        marker = "**",
        depth = 2,
        instruction = "The most difficult color to obtain is Red. Hot spells and heat waves are more frequent in the game's summer months, although random hot spells can pop up any time of the game year.",
        action = "note",
        entities = {  },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = { "unknown-template:fire" },
      },
      {
        order = 46,
        marker = "***",
        depth = 3,
        instruction = "You can check the in-game month by using the /clock command (identical to Menu -> Current Time). Note that the command is a toggle that shows/hides the compass, day, time, and pos in the lower left of the screen, so you'll want to use it twice to get back into the same state your client was in.",
        action = "note",
        entities = {  },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 47,
        marker = "***",
        depth = 3,
        instruction = "Weather is the same across the zone, and sometimes identical in other zones nearby.",
        action = "note",
        entities = {  },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 48,
        marker = "****",
        depth = 4,
        instruction = "For example, Rabao, Western, & Eastern Altepa Desert all have identical weather, so checking one is the same as checking all. These groupings are known as \"Areas\" at a Weather Forecast NPC.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Rabao", "Western Altepa Desert", "Eastern Altepa Desert", "Weather Forecast" },
        zones = { "Rabao", "Eastern Altepa Desert", "Western Altepa Desert" },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 49,
        marker = "*****",
        depth = 5,
        instruction = "While you can't get the scene in Rabao due to it being a non-Field area, you can use Home Point #1 there as your warp destination to see it periodically first-hand. From here, you can walk outside the entrance or use the nearby survival guide to jump into one of the zones.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Rabao" },
        zones = { "Rabao" },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 50,
        marker = "****",
        depth = 4,
        instruction = "Weather is not necessarily the same across the region as a whole, see Zulkheim having 3 distinct weathers. Also, weather patterns aren't necessarily bound by region lines either - see Elshimo Uplands & Lowlands sharing their weather trends for Yhoator & Yuhtunga Jungles as well as Kazham.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Zulkheim", "Elshimo Uplands", "Elshimo Lowlands", "Yhoator Jungle", "Yuhtunga Jungle", "Kazham" },
        zones = { "Kazham", "Yhoator Jungle", "Yuhtunga Jungle" },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 51,
        marker = "***",
        depth = 3,
        instruction = "It is worth noting that Red weather also tends to be more prevalent around midday (12:00 noon) in the relevant zone. So if you are having difficulty finding this weather, try in the middle of the day rather than checking during nighttime.",
        action = "note",
        entities = {  },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 52,
        marker = "***",
        depth = 3,
        instruction = "In addition to time of day and the season: A Firesday appears to make it more probable to encounter fire weather. Hence: checking zones on that day is advised. (Especially Eastern Altepa Desert, Western Altepa Desert and Valkurm Dunes)",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Firesday", "Eastern Altepa Desert", "Western Altepa Desert", "Valkurm Dunes" },
        zones = { "Eastern Altepa Desert", "Western Altepa Desert", "Valkurm Dunes" },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
        order = 53,
        marker = "***",
        depth = 3,
        instruction = "The pre-Zilart field areas where fire weather & Fire Elementals spawn were mainly used by Japanese players who didn't have the expansion pack, as SMN was released as a one-off job but not actually part of the Zilart expansion. In the modern game, almost all players will have the expansion (English players have had it since launch), but these areas might be still... Required details: Fire Elemental, SMN, Free Trial.",
        action = "note",
        entities = { "Fire Elemental", "SMN", "Free Trial" },
        zones = {  },
        map_numbers = {  },
        grid_coordinates = {  },
        items = {  },
        key_items = {  },
        warnings = {  },
      },
      {
